From: Cubie A7S bringup <local>
Subject: [PATCH] media: sunxi-vin: wire up the orphan imx415 sensor driver

bsp/drivers/vin/modules/sensor/imx415_mipi.c is present in the Armbian
sun60iw2 kernel tree (linux-orangepi orange-pi-6.6-sun60iw2, 33487 bytes) and
already carries the 6.6 API guards, but nothing ever compiles it:

  * the sensor Kconfig has no SENSOR_IMX415 symbol, and
  * the sensor Makefile has no obj-$(CONFIG_SENSOR_IMX415) line,

so Radxa's Camera 4K (IMX415) can never work, even though Radxa's own BSP
branch already wires it up (radxa/allwinner-bsp@cubie-aiot-v1.4.8 has
"config SENSOR_IMX415" in Kconfig and "obj-$(CONFIG_SENSOR_IMX415) +=
imx415_mipi.o" in the Makefile, and Radxa's 5.15 image ships
CONFIG_SENSOR_IMX415=m).

Upstream context: radxa/allwinner-bsp@cubie-aiot-v1.4.8 does wire this driver
up (config SENSOR_IMX415 with prompt "use imx415 driver" at Kconfig:155 and
obj-$(CONFIG_SENSOR_IMX415) += imx415_mipi.o at Makefile:39), but the newer
cubie-aiot-v1.5.0 branch DROPPED it again, and the tree Armbian builds for this
family inherited that state.  This patch restores the last known-good wiring,
prompt text included.

Add the missing symbol right before SENSOR_IMX477 -- the position the driver
occupies in Radxa's tree and in the 5.15 config -- plus the matching Makefile
line.  Note the Kconfig prompt ("use imx415 driver") is *not* what the camera
overlay matches on: the overlay's sensor0_mname = "imx415_mipi" matches the
driver name the module registers (SENSOR_NAME below), not the prompt text.

The driver registers two i2c driver names, "imx415_mipi" and "imx415_mipi_2"
(SENSOR_NUM == 2), which is how the module exposes the 1-lane and 2-lane
variants of the part.

Baseline (verified against the real build tree, not a stand-in):
  linux-orangepi orange-pi-6.6-sun60iw2
    bsp/drivers/vin/modules/sensor/Kconfig   md5 b9eebae1b300
    bsp/drivers/vin/modules/sensor/Makefile  md5 d54f47b9c643
  (Kconfig: SENSOR_IMX326 at :155, SENSOR_IMX477 at :159
   Makefile: SENSOR_IMX326 at :39,  SENSOR_IMX477 at :40)

Signed-off-by: Cubie A7S bringup <local>
---
diff --git a/bsp/drivers/vin/modules/sensor/Kconfig b/bsp/drivers/vin/modules/sensor/Kconfig
--- a/bsp/drivers/vin/modules/sensor/Kconfig
+++ b/bsp/drivers/vin/modules/sensor/Kconfig
@@ -156,6 +156,10 @@
 	tristate "use imx326 driver"
 	default n
 
+config SENSOR_IMX415
+	tristate "use imx415 driver"
+	default n
+
 config SENSOR_IMX477
 	tristate "use imx477 driver"
 	default n
 
diff --git a/bsp/drivers/vin/modules/sensor/Makefile b/bsp/drivers/vin/modules/sensor/Makefile
--- a/bsp/drivers/vin/modules/sensor/Makefile
+++ b/bsp/drivers/vin/modules/sensor/Makefile
@@ -37,6 +37,7 @@
 obj-$(CONFIG_SENSOR_IMX317)			+= imx317_mipi.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_SENSOR_IMX335)			+= imx335_mipi.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_SENSOR_IMX326)			+= imx326_mipi.o
+obj-$(CONFIG_SENSOR_IMX415)			+= imx415_mipi.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_SENSOR_IMX477)			+= imx477_mipi.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_SENSOR_OV2710)			+= ov2710_mipi.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_SENSOR_OV2718)			+= ov2718_mipi.o
 
